{"slug": "yvonne-maffeis-dates-with-cream-and-chopped-pistachios", "nyt_id": 1017466, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1017466-yvonne-maffeis-dates-with-cream-and-chopped-pistachios", "name": "Yvonne Maffei’s Dates With Cream and Chopped Pistachios", "author": "Julia Moskin", "description": "Dates and dairy are ancient staples of the Middle East. This recipe, from Yvonne Maffei, who writes the popular cooking and nutrition blog My Halal Kitchen, combines the two into a luxurious dessert, for Ramadan or other feasts, with very little effort from the cook. Julia Moskin", "servings": {"text": "6 to 12 servings", "min": 6, "max": 12, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "PT20M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "12 large medjool dates", "group": null, "quantity": 12.0, "unit": null, "item": "large medjool dates", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "24 whole almonds (preferably blanched), walnuts or pecans", "group": null, "quantity": 24.0, "unit": null, "item": "whole almonds", "preparation": "walnuts or pecans", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "3 to 4 tablespoons crème fraîche", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "crème fraîche", "preparation": null, "optional": false, "quantity_max": 4.0}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Freshly grated zest of 1 lemon or ½ orange (about 2 teaspoons)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly grated zest of 1 lemon or ½ orange", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 tablespoon coarsely chopped pistachios", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "coarsely chopped pistachios", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Rinse and dry the dates. Make a clean cut along the side of each date to open, and remove the pit."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Stuff each date with 2 whole almonds and lightly pinch closed. (The recipe can be made up to this point up to 2 days in advance. Store in an airtight container.)"}, {"position": 3, "text": "When ready to serve, arrange dates cut sides up on a plate or platter. Drizzle on the crème fraîche, making a dollop on each date. Sprinkle on the citrus zest, then the chopped pistachios. Serve immediately, as finger food or on plates with a small fork and knife."}], "nutrition": null, "tags": {"cuisine": ["middle-eastern"], "diet": [], "course": ["dessert-snack"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["almond", "cr-me-fra-che", "five-ingredient", "medjool-date", "quick", "ramadan"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2015/06/17/dining/17MAFFEI/17MAFFEI-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2015/06/17/dining/17MAFFEI/17MAFFEI-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 394}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2015-06-17", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T03:40:35Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "yvonne-maffeis-roast-chicken-with-couscous-dates-and-buttered-almonds", "nyt_id": 1017467, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1017467-yvonne-maffeis-roast-chicken-with-couscous-dates-and-buttered-almonds", "name": "Yvonne Maffei’s Roast Chicken With Couscous, Dates and Buttered Almonds", "author": "Julia Moskin", "description": "Deglet Noors dates shine when they are cooked in chutneys, desserts or North African dishes like this whole roast chicken. The chicken is cooked with fluffy couscous that absorbs the sweetness of dates and the butteriness of toasted almonds. Supermarket Deglet Noors are often dark brown and hard, because they have been kept well past their natural point of ripeness; seek out soft, light-colored ones for the best flavor. Julia Moskin", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 90, "raw": {"total": "PT1H30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "4 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 tablespoons fresh lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fresh lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ teaspoon ground ginger", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground ginger", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "½ teaspoon ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Fine sea salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "fine sea salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 large whole chicken, about 4 pounds", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large whole chicken", "preparation": "about 4 pounds", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 cups couscous (not instant)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "couscous", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "3 tablespoons butter", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ cup sliced almonds", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "sliced almonds", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "½ cup slivered dates", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "slivered dates", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 teaspoon sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 teaspoon ground cinnamon", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cinnamon", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "2 tablespoons orange blossom water (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "orange blossom water", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 14, "raw": "2 tablespoons honey", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "honey", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "Chopped mint, parsley or cilantro, or a combination, for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "chopped mint", "preparation": "parsley or cilantro, or a combination, for garnish", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat oven to 375 degrees. In a large ovenproof dish or pot with a tight lid, combine 2 tablespoons olive oil, the lemon juice, the ginger, the pepper and 1 teaspoon salt. Add the chicken and rub it around in the mixture until evenly coated. Turn chicken breast side down and roast, uncovered, for 50 minutes."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Meanwhile, in a large bowl, combine couscous, 2 cups water and ½ teaspoon salt. Set aside for 5 to 15 minutes to soak."}, {"position": 3, "text": "In a small skillet, melt the butter. Add almonds and cook, stirring constantly, just until toasted and golden; adjust heat so almonds and butter do not scorch. Turn off heat and stir in dates."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Add almond-date mixture to couscous, along with any butter left in pan, and mix, fluffing the grains with a fork. Mix in 2 tablespoons olive oil, the sugar, the cinnamon and the orange blossom water (if using)."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Drizzle or paint honey over top of chicken (leave chicken breast-side down in pot). Add couscous mixture to the pot, arranging it around the chicken. Cover tightly with a lid or foil and return to the oven for 30 minutes more."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Remove from the oven. When cool enough to handle, remove chicken and carve into serving pieces. Stir and fluff couscous, scraping up any chicken skin stuck to bottom of pan, and place chicken pieces back on top of couscous. Sprinkle with chopped herbs and serve immediately."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 912.8333333333334, "protein_g": 65.7, "carbohydrates_g": 67.8, "fat_g": 64.7, "saturated_fat_g": 18.2, "unsaturated_fat_g": 12.0, "trans_fat_g": 0.3, "cholesterol_mg": 242.1, "sodium_mg": 1046.9, "fiber_g": 5.4, "sugar_g": 19.4, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-lunch-main-course-roasts"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["almond", "chicken", "couscous", "date", "orange-blossom-water", "ramadan"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2015/06/17/dining/17JPRAMADAN3/17JPRAMADAN3-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600-v2.jpg", "alt": "Roast chicken with couscous, dates and buttered almonds.", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2015/06/17/dining/17JPRAMADAN3/17JPRAMADAN3-superJumbo-v3.jpg", "alt": "Roast chicken with couscous, dates and buttered almonds.", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2015/06/17/dining/17JPRAMADAN3/17JPRAMADAN3-facebookJumbo-v3.jpg", "alt": "Roast chicken with couscous, dates and buttered almonds.", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 1855}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2015-06-17", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T03:40:37Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
